# L §7.2 table of modes: down toward zero; up away from zero; floor toward −∞; ceil toward +∞; half-up the nearest,
# a tie away from zero; half-down the nearest, a tie toward zero; half-even the nearest, a tie to the even
# multiple.  Columns in that order, step 1, for 2.5, −2.5, 3.5, 2.4 and −2.6.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index ks = [a, b, c, d, e]
input x[k in ks]: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[a] = 2.5
  x[b] = -2.5
  x[c] = 3.5
  x[d] = 2.4
  x[e] = -2.6

ask q1: round(x[k], 1, down), round(x[k], 1, up), round(x[k], 1, floor), round(x[k], 1, ceil), round(x[k], 1, half-up), round(x[k], 1, half-down), round(x[k], 1, half-even) for k in ks
=== expect
q1 (k = a): (2, 3, 2, 3, 3, 2, 2)
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = b): (-2, -3, -3, -2, -3, -2, -2)
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = c): (3, 4, 3, 4, 4, 3, 4)
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = d): (2, 3, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2)
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = e): (-2, -3, -3, -2, -3, -3, -3)
  cut 2026-12-31
